@startuml ad_finder_sequence_diagram
title Home Search Bar — Live AD Finder + Unlock + Password Reset

actor User
participant "FinderPresenter" as Presenter
participant "MainPresenter\n(reset overlay)" as Shell
participant "DispatcherTimer\n(debounce / poll)" as Timer
participant "AdSearchWorker.ps1\n(one per forest, on pool)" as Worker
participant "ActiveDirectoryService" as AD
participant "AdUnlockWorker.ps1" as Unlock
participant "AdResetPasswordWorker.ps1" as Reset
participant "LensLookupWorker.ps1\n(-OwnerOf batch, on pool)" as OwnerWorker

User -> Presenter: Type prefix (>= MinPrefix chars)
activate Presenter
Presenter -> Presenter: OnSearchTextChanged()
Presenter -> Timer: restart debounce
deactivate Presenter

Timer -> Presenter: debounce elapsed -> RunAdSearch()
activate Presenter
Presenter -> Presenter: AbortSearch() (bump SearchToken)
loop one job per forest
    Presenter -> Worker: BeginInvoke(prefix, domain) on pool
    activate Worker
    Worker -> AD: Search(prefix)
    activate AD
    AD -> AD: QueryDirectory() via DirectorySearcher\n(computers + users, AdFilter)
    AD --> Worker: AdSearchResult[]
    deactivate AD
    Worker --> Presenter: (async) rows for this forest
    deactivate Worker
end
Presenter -> Timer: start poll timer
deactivate Presenter

loop poll until every forest lands
    Timer -> Presenter: PollSearch()
    activate Presenter
    note right of Presenter: Discard stale-token results;\ndedupe by Kind|Domain|Sam;\nAdSearchRank.Order ranks computers and\nusers by which field prefix-matched;\nrender the growing union.
    Presenter -> User: Dropdown — COMPUTERS + USERS\n(every user shows "Reset...";\nlocked users add "Unlock")
    deactivate Presenter
end

alt Pick a computer
    User -> Presenter: Click computer
    Presenter -> Presenter: OnPickComputer() -> add host row + prefetch
else Unlock a locked user
    User -> Presenter: Click "Unlock"
    Presenter -> Unlock: BeginInvoke(sam, domain) on pool
    activate Unlock
    Unlock -> AD: UnlockUser(user)
    AD --> Unlock: success
    Unlock --> Presenter: (async) result
    deactivate Unlock
    Presenter -> User: Toast "Account unlocked"
else Reset a user's password
    User -> Presenter: Click "Reset..."
    Presenter -> Shell: OnShowReset seam -> ShowReset(user)
    Shell -> User: Reset overlay (type or Generate;\nCopy / QR; change-at-logon pre-checked)
    User -> Shell: "Reset password"
    Shell -> Reset: RunOnPool(sam, domain,\nSecureString, changeAtLogon)
    activate Reset
    Reset -> AD: ResetPassword(user, pwd, flag)
    note right of AD: Set-ADAccountPassword -Reset\n+ Set-ADUser -ChangePasswordAtLogon.\nThe password is never logged.
    AD --> Reset: success
    Reset --> Shell: (async) result
    deactivate Reset
    Shell -> User: Toast; overlay stays open\n(closing wipes the secret)
end

== Machine-owner batch (background, single-flight) ==
Presenter -> OwnerWorker: ResolveOwners(machines) ->\nBeginInvoke(-OwnerOf batch) on pool
note right of Presenter: HomePresenter asks once for every listed\nmachine missing an owner; one in-flight\nbatch (OwnerJob), reaped on the Lens poll\ntick (ReapOwners).
OwnerWorker --> Presenter: (async) owners bundle (machine -> owner)
Presenter -> User: owner chip on each card\n(HostViewModel.SetOwner)
note right of Presenter: Owners persist via\nRecentConnectionsStore.UpsertOwner\n(config\\recents.json),\nsaves coalesced by DeferSave.
@enduml
